so the infinite game and the internet  mindset is not the absence of the finite  game it's the context within which the  finite game exists and so we overuse  sports analogies and war analogies in  business which as you pointed out very  often our finite nature definitely  sports most of the time a war and so I  go back to my metaphor a moment ago  which is we need to adjust our mindset  to understand what business actually is  which is it's a lifestyle so we can have  finite goals we can have arbitrary goals  set to arbitrary dates I want to lose X  amount of weight by X date and you work  really hard to metrics are really  important you know as tangibly driven  animals we need to be able to count  metrics it makes us feel like we're  making progress really really important  and so I'm doing all the right things  and I'm measuring myself and I hit my  goal on the date and the problem is I  have to keep doing it now every single  day for the rest of my life it doesn't  end business is the same even if we hit  our goals we have to keep going so what  the infinite game provides is what is  this all for this has there has to be  something bigger than just hitting these  dates conversely if we miss our goal you  know what happens nothing nothing  happens in fact if we've been building a  good business if we've been living a  healthy lifestyle we're way better off  now than we were when we started and if  we just keep on this path we'll hit our  goal in another month or two right and  so I think one of the things that the  infinite game provides and how we do how  we conduct business at the frontline is  not just is not just the finite metrics  it's not just did we hit the goal on the  date but rather how did we get there  what's the trend data did we get there  in an ethical way are we promoting  people who who are building a strong  company for the long term for the  infinite or are we only promoting people  who hit the arbitrary number in the  arbitrary date we only evaluate so too  often we evaluate someone's performance  but we don't evaluate what kind of  character they have and so many  businesses so many leaders and  businesses will know that there's a  toxic team member but their numbers are  so good so we just let them keep their  job  as opposed to sitting down with them  coaching them or eventually removing  them regardless of what their numbers  are at the end of the day though the  front line has to be more preoccupied  with the finite game right because there  are beginning middles and ends for them  so let's take an airline analogy we  absolutely want those gate agents  obsessed with the finite game we want a  beginning middle and end we want that  plane to leave on time and then they'll  repeat the process but we need them to  be aware of the infinite game we need  them to understand that this company  needs to survive beyond this flight in  other words they need to treat the  customers nicely because they want the  customers to want to come back as  opposed to just getting this flight off  off the line on the time and and then  and then be done with it and we hear  that all the time I'm just doing my job  right like this is what we have to do  and this is sort of where bureaucracy  seeps in because bureaucrats don't care  about the infinite game they're just  trying to follow what's in front of them  but as we make our way through the ranks  at the senior level and you touched upon  this we have to become more obsessed  with the infinite game we have to become  obsessed with understanding how all  these pieces of the puzzle contribute to  the long game and how sometimes we're  gonna have to make decisions that hurt  us in the short term because it's the  right thing to do for the long term and  that's really hard to do and when you  have senior leaders who are overly  obsessed with the finite game then they  just make short decisions that are good  for now that actually do long-term  damage but at the frontlines we need our  people to understand what the vision is  we want them to be involved we want them  to work on trusting teams we want them  to start learning leadership so as they  work their way through the ranks  they bring that infinite mindset with  them as they come  [Music]
 

